    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/08/asics-megablast-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The 45/37 mm FF Turbo Squared midsole is well-cushioned and bouncy with a balanced firm-soft feel; impact protection is strong, the heel transition is smooth (good bevel), and the forefoot feels stiffer with limited flex.",
        "Responsiveness: Ride is highly energetic and snappy, with clear bounce/energy return that increases when pace picks up, making it especially strong for uptempo and long efforts.",
        "Stability: Stability is only moderate (explicitly less stable than Superblast); the high-stack, performance-focused geometry feels less controlled, though heel hold is secure from the semi-structured/flexible padded heel counter and traction is very secure in turns/wet conditions.",
        "Durability: Stated durability expectation is normal; ASICSGRIP outsole shows excellent grip and confidence in wet surfaces, but no specific long-term outsole wear issues or upper longevity concerns were reported."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/09/asics-megablast-review-5-comparisons.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The 45/37 mm FF Turbo Squared midsole is described as plush/soft with strong impact protection, feeling soft to the touch but relatively firm underfoot; heel hold is secure, while forefoot toe-off can feel a bit labored at slower paces.",
        "Responsiveness: Ride is repeatedly called bouncy, lively, and high-energy, with claimed improvements (about 32% bouncier) and good energy return across paces after a short break-in.",
        "Stability: Stability is mixed—some testers found the platform stable and smooth through gait, but others reported it is not particularly stable because of the soft foam, very light upper, and minimal/gusset-related tongue support.",
        "Durability: Outsole rubber is strategically placed with good thickness and strong grip (including wet traction), and reviewers expect solid durability despite some exposed midsole foam."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/asics-megablast-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The 45 mm heel / 37 mm forefoot stack and new Flytefoam Turbo Squared are described as soft and bouncy, pointing to strong impact protection with a max-cushion feel.",
        "Responsiveness: Flytefoam Turbo Squared is positioned as \"ultimate bounce\" (claimed ~33% bouncier than FF Turbo), and the ride is repeatedly described as lively.",
        "Stability: The shoe can feel a little blocky, while the more structured woven upper and padded heel collar are noted to help lock the heel in place.",
        "Durability: The review ties Megablast to Superblast-like reliability and \"hundreds of miles\" longevity, with AsicsGrip called Asics' best outsole rubber."
      ]
    }
